@startuml SABER Inspect AI Integration Sequence

!theme plain
title SABER + Inspect AI Integration - Evaluation Workflow

actor "User" as User
participant "inspect CLI" as InspectCLI
participant "Domain Task\n(cybench.py)" as DomainTask
participant "create_domain_task" as TaskFactory
participant "DomainController" as DomainCtrl
participant "SABERSandboxEnvironment" as Sandbox
participant "ClientSessionManager" as SessionMgr
participant "create_saber_dataset" as Dataset
participant "saber_scorer" as Scorer
participant "SABER Server" as Server
participant "MCP Tools" as MCP

User -> InspectCLI: inspect eval domains/cybench --model openai/gpt-4

note right of User
**User Command**
Standard Inspect AI command
with domain task path
end note

InspectCLI -> DomainTask: Load task module
activate DomainTask

DomainTask -> TaskFactory: @task\ncybench(**kwargs)
activate TaskFactory

note over TaskFactory
**Task Factory Execution**
- Extract parameters from kwargs
- Setup domain configuration
- Initialize server controller
end note

TaskFactory -> DomainCtrl: Start SABER domain server
activate DomainCtrl

DomainCtrl -> Server: saber-domain start cybench
activate Server

note right of Server
**Server Launch**
- Loads domain.yaml manifest
- Initializes BenchmarkManager
- Starts REST API (port 8000)
- Starts MCP API (port 8001)
end note

DomainCtrl -> Server: Health check (wait for ready)
Server --> DomainCtrl: Healthy

note over TaskFactory, SessionMgr
**Initialize Client Session**
end note

TaskFactory -> SessionMgr: Create session
activate SessionMgr
SessionMgr -> Server: POST /api/v1/session
Server --> SessionMgr: session_id
SessionMgr --> TaskFactory: ClientSessionManager instance

note over TaskFactory, Dataset
**Load Dataset from Server**
end note

TaskFactory -> Dataset: create_saber_dataset(session_mgr, task_filter)
activate Dataset
Dataset -> SessionMgr: get_tasks()
SessionMgr -> Server: GET /api/v1/tasks
Server --> SessionMgr: BenchmarkInfo
SessionMgr --> Dataset: List[TaskInfo]

Dataset -> Dataset: Convert TaskInfo → inspect_ai.Sample
note right of Dataset
Each Sample contains:
- task_id
- instruction_prompt
- assistant_prompt
- submit_prompt
- SABER metadata
end note

Dataset --> TaskFactory: List[Sample]
deactivate Dataset

note over TaskFactory, Sandbox
**Create Sandbox Environment**
end note

TaskFactory -> Sandbox: SABERSandboxEnvironment(domain, session_mgr)
activate Sandbox
Sandbox --> TaskFactory: Sandbox instance

note over TaskFactory, Scorer
**Create Scorer**
end note

TaskFactory -> Scorer: saber_scorer(session_mgr)
activate Scorer
Scorer --> TaskFactory: Scorer instance

TaskFactory -> TaskFactory: Build Task(dataset, sandbox, scorer)
TaskFactory --> DomainTask: Inspect AI Task
deactivate TaskFactory
DomainTask --> InspectCLI: Task

note over InspectCLI
**Inspect AI Execution**
For each sample in dataset:
end note

loop For each sample

    InspectCLI -> Sandbox: sample_init(sample)
    Sandbox -> SessionMgr: create_episode(task_id)
    SessionMgr -> Server: POST /api/v1/session/{id}/episodes
    Server --> SessionMgr: episode_id, environment_spec
    SessionMgr --> Sandbox: episode_id

    Sandbox -> Sandbox: Store episode_id and metadata
    note right of Sandbox
    Stores episode_id, task_id,
    and MCP context for tool calls
    end note

    Sandbox --> InspectCLI: SandboxEnvironmentSpec

    note over InspectCLI
    **Agent Execution**
    Inspect AI runs agent
    (e.g., ReAct, custom agent)
    end note

    loop Agent Steps
        InspectCLI -> InspectCLI: Agent generates tool call
        InspectCLI -> MCP: Execute SABER MCP tool
        activate MCP

        note right of MCP
        Inspect AI uses mcp_server_http()
        with headers containing:
        - X-SABER-Session-ID
        - X-SABER-Episode-ID
        - X-SABER-Orchestration-Env
        end note

        MCP -> Server: MCP tool call with context headers
        Server -> Server: Execute command in episode sandbox
        Server --> MCP: Command result
        deactivate MCP

        MCP --> InspectCLI: Tool result
    end

    note over InspectCLI, Scorer
    **Scoring**
    end note

    InspectCLI -> Scorer: score(state, target)
    Scorer -> Scorer: Get episode_id from store
    Scorer -> SessionMgr: get_evaluation(episode_id)
    SessionMgr -> Server: GET /api/v1/evaluation/{episode_id}
    Server -> Server: Evaluate episode\n(submission + steps)
    Server --> SessionMgr: EvaluationResponse
    SessionMgr --> Scorer: Evaluation data

    Scorer -> Scorer: Create Score object\n(value, explanation, metadata)
    Scorer --> InspectCLI: Score

    note over InspectCLI, Sandbox
    **Episode Cleanup**
    end note

    InspectCLI -> Sandbox: sample_cleanup()
    Sandbox -> SessionMgr: end_episode(episode_id)
    SessionMgr -> Server: DELETE /api/v1/session/{id}/episodes/{eid}
    Server -> Server: Cleanup episode resources
    Server --> SessionMgr: Success
    SessionMgr --> Sandbox: Success

end

note over InspectCLI
**Evaluation Complete**
All samples processed
end note

InspectCLI -> Sandbox: task_cleanup()
Sandbox -> SessionMgr: terminate_session()
SessionMgr -> Server: DELETE /api/v1/session/{id}
Server --> SessionMgr: Success

Sandbox -> DomainCtrl: stop_domain() (if stop_saber_after=true)
DomainCtrl -> Server: saber-domain stop cybench
deactivate Server
deactivate DomainCtrl

deactivate Sandbox
deactivate Scorer
deactivate SessionMgr
deactivate DomainTask

InspectCLI --> User: EvalLog results

note over User
**Results**
- Per-sample scores
- Aggregate metrics
- Logs saved to .inspect_ai/logs/
end note

@enduml
